You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 2. Task data model + JSON persistence
Objective: Define a typed task model and persist it safely to JSON storage.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Provide a minimal Bun-based CLI entrypoint and command surface for TaskForge so future study tasks can plug into a stable interface.
Decisions: Use Bun runtime with a shebang entry at src/cli.ts (#!/usr/bin/env bun); Keep a small, explicit command registry: help, version, run, list; Implement a lightweight, custom argv parser reading Bun.argv and normalizing flags vs positionals; Keep handlers modular under src/commands/*.ts and dispatch via a simple router; Source version from package.json at runtime or fall back to a temporary constant; Add Bun dev scripts in package.json (e.g. bun run src/cli.ts --help) and optionally a bin mapping for installability
Risks: Overbuilding the parser too early may complicate future command surface changes; Bun-specific argv/runtime assumptions could hurt portability if Node support is later required; Reading package.json at runtime for version may be brittle depending on packaging/build layout
Snippets: #!/usr/bin/env bun | const argv = Bun.argv.slice(1);
// normalize flags vs positionals
const flags = {}; const positionals = [];
for (const a of argv) { if (a.startsWith('--')) flags[a.replace(/^--/, '')]=true; else if (a.startsWith('-')) flags[a.replace(/^-+/,'')]=true; else positionals.push(a) } | const commands = {
  help: await import('./commands/help'),
  version: await import('./commands/version'),
  run: await import('./commands/run'),
  list: await import('./commands/list')
}; | const cmd = positionals[0] || (flags.help ? 'help' : undefined);
if (!cmd || !commands[cmd]) { console.error('Unknown command'); process.exit(2) }
await commands[cmd].handler({ flags, positionals: positionals.slice(1) }); | const version = (()=>{ try{ return JSON.parse(Bun.readFileSync('package.json').toString()).version }catch(e){ return '0.0.0' } })();
